      "text_raw": "This is an experimental\nresult for a two-stage\nopamp, with a GBW of\n1 MHz.\nIt is clear that second-\norder distortion is domi-\nnant. It is generated by the\noutput stage. Its slope is\nclose to 40 dB/decade as\nexpected.\nThe third-order distortion\nis visible at higher frequen-\ncies but never dominant. Its\nslope is even higher.\nFor frequencies lower\nthan about 7 kHz, the dis-\ntortions drown in the noise. No reliable measurements of distortion are possible here.",
      "text": "This is an experimental result for a two-stage opamp, with a GBW of 1 MHz. It is clear that secondorder distortion is dominant. It is generated by the output stage. Its slope is close to 40 dB/decade as expected. The third-order distortion is visible at higher frequencies but never dominant. Its slope is even higher. For frequencies lower than about 7 kHz, the distortions drown in the noise. No reliable measurements of distortion are possible here."
    }
